{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Ho.</b> An expression of call, and the meaning is concerning those who do not believe the words of HaShem, who said: these are the things to come." "<b>Rav.</b> He quarrels with his maker, and this 'maker' is like ככלי יוצר תנפצם (Psalms 2:9)." "<b>Choref.</b> For it is understood as a plower who plows the ground." "<b>Will clay say to its maker, what are you making.</b> This is impossible; rather, the maker does his will." "Or he says <b>your deed has no hands</b>, or he says to the maker: this that you made, your hands did not make it. But the correct interpretation is that it is doubled, and the meaning is: your deed was made without hands, for you have no dominion over it to do your will."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:09.587261408Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}